{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>A rejoicing heart</b>, גֵּהָה — it lacks [the letter] kaf of רפאה (healing), meaning: the heart that rejoices in its portion does good for the body like גהה, because its natural disposition is to rejoice, as in 'לֹא יִגְהֶה מִכֶּם' (it will not depart from you). But a spirit that is suffering and angry over the vanities of the world dries the bone, which is the foundation of the body, and גהה is of no avail for it."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:24.392765643Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}